// Parity: assert_eq / assert_ne success path.
//
// This test forces the lowered builtin (and the C runtime helper
// rt_assert_eq_fail) to be referenced by the AOT object, but never
// actually triggers the failure branch. The point is to confirm the
// linker can resolve rt_assert_eq_fail at AOT link time — for a long
// time the symbol was registered in the JIT but missing from the C
// runtime, which broke any AOT build that used assert_eq/assert_ne.
fn main() {
    assert_eq(1 + 1, 2)
    assert_eq("turbo", "turbo")
    assert_eq(true, true)
    assert_ne(1, 2)
    assert_ne("a", "b")
    print("ok")
}
